 "cash_tip": "Locals say Sayulita ATMs charge high fees, so use a bank ATM rather than a standalone one, always choose 'decline conversion' so you're charged in pesos, and take out a larger amount once instead of several small withdrawals. Keep small bills handy for tacos, taxis and the market, and if you happen to be in San Pancho, the hospital ATM there is the cheapest for US cards at about 60 pesos.",
